UID:mO2Q2TNsRh
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 195 mins (3h15m)\n\nThe Emerald City Short Film Fest
 ival is a new film festival devoted to showcasing filmmakers local to Wash
 ington and helping foster a diverse and welcoming community of filmmakers 
 and movie enthusiasts. $10 ($7 SIFF Members and Students)\n\nhttps://www.s
 iff.net/cinema/in-theaters/emerald-city-short-film-festival
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tim Travers and the Time Traveler’s Paradox
DTSTART:20250809T020000Z
DTEND:20250809T040500Z
DTSTAMP:20250809T020000Z
UID:JdbkLuxyYM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 103 mins (1h43m)\n\nIn this blast of WA state scienc
 e fiction co-starring Felicia Day (“Mystery Science Theater 3000”)\, K
 eith David (The Thing)\, and Seattle native Joel McHale (“Community”)\
 , a brilliant scientist invents a time machine and concocts a scheme to ki
 ll his younger self…with unintended consequences. Post-film Q&A on Augus
 t 8 with director Stimson Snead.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theate
 rs/tim-travers-and-the-time-travelers-paradox
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
